# Cloudflare Pages / Netlify redirect fixture.
#
# Exercises source 2 of utils/retired-versions.html: a retired version is
# recognized because something redirects away from it with `?fromversion=`,
# with no [[params.versions]] entry and no params.retiredVersions line.
#
# Lives under fixture/ and is mounted to `static` by the fixture configs, so
# consumers importing this module never receive it. A real `_redirects` at the
# repo's top-level static/ WOULD be mounted into every consumer's site root and
# would change their hosting behavior.

# A retirement. v0 appears nowhere else in the fixture config — the notice
# firing for it is the whole point of the test.
/v0/*  /v2/:splat?fromversion=v0  301

# An ordinary redirect with no marker. Must contribute nothing: a moved page is
# not a retired version, which is why the parameter is opt-in per rule.
/moved-page/  /v2/everything/  301

# Commented out, and must stay ignored. A rule someone disabled should not keep
# claiming its version is retired.
# /v00/*  /v2/:splat?fromversion=v00  301

# Multiple parameters, marker first. The extractor terminates on `&`, so this
# contributes "v0multi" rather than "v0multi&foo=bar".
/v0multi/*  /v2/:splat?fromversion=v0multi&foo=bar  301
